      "comment": "OUR SWEET JEANNIE (8) did a good job to finish third two starts ago then registered a commanding victory last start, coming wider on this row and racing wide in the latter stages before scoring by 5.5 metres at Shepparton. Shouldn't spend a penny from this draw and the sprint lane may come in handy. Could strike again. HANDLER (5) came from this barrier to place here two back then chased a smart one and finished fourth last start at this circuit and distance. Has ability and should be right in the finish. BREATHE EASY (1) looks well served by the ace draw and could be close to a win after coming from wider barriers to place in his last three outings, two of them here. COOL STORY (7) did some work last time but scored back-to-back wins from second line draws prior so is worth another chance.",
